---
source: packages/tier1/plot/tests/printing.rs
expression: all
---
== no_place
error[Z0406]: `hline` needs `at`
 --> scripts/main.zeff:3:28
  |
3 | d.plot(x: dose, y: change).hline()
  |                            ^^^^^ `at` is missing
  |
  = help: a reference line stands at a number on the `y` axis, as in `hline(at: 0)`, or at each value of a variable, as in `hline(at: wage)`

== a_place_that_is_text
error[Z0401]: `vline` draws a line at each value of `at:` on the `x` axis, so `arm` must be a Bool, Int, Float, Date or DateTime variable, but it is a Str
 --> scripts/main.zeff:3:38
  |
3 | d.plot(x: dose, y: change).vline(at: arm)
  |                                      ^^^ not a number or a date
  |
  = help: a reference line stands at a number or at a date; `d.describe()` lists the types of the variables

== a_place_in_quotes
error[Z0401]: `at` of `hline` must be a Float, Date, DateTime or Var, but this is a Str
 --> scripts/main.zeff:3:38
  |
3 | d.plot(x: dose, y: change).hline(at: "0")
  |                                      ^^^ a Str
  |
  = help: usage: `p.hline(data: Frame, at: Float | Date | DateTime | Var, color: Var | Str, style: solid | dashed | dotted | dash_dot | long_dash | dash_dot_dot = dashed, width: Float = 0.5)`

== no_such_variable
error[Z0101]: no variable `chnge` in `d`
 --> scripts/main.zeff:3:38
  |
3 | d.plot(x: dose, y: change).hline(at: chnge)
  |                                      ^^^^^ not a variable of d
  |
  = help: did you mean `change`? If you meant a category level, write it in quotes: `"change"`

== a_binding_of_text_is_not_a_place
error[Z0101]: no variable `centre` in `d`
 --> scripts/main.zeff:4:38
  |
4 | d.plot(x: dose, y: change).hline(at: centre)
  |                                      ^^^^^^ not a variable of d
  |
  = help: the variables of `d` are: dose, change, arm

== an_infinite_place
error[Z0401]: `at:` of `hline` is a place on the `y` axis, but this is Inf
 --> scripts/main.zeff:3:38
  |
3 | d.plot(x: dose, y: change).hline(at: 1e308 * 10)
  |                                      ^^^^^^^^^^ not a place on the axis
  |
  = help: a reference line stands at a finite number, or at each value of a variable

== no_axis_for_the_line
error[Z0401]: `hline` draws a line at a place on the `y` axis, but nothing is mapped to `y` yet
 --> scripts/main.zeff:3:17
  |
3 | d.plot(x: dose).hline(at: 0)
  |                 ^^^^^ needs a `y` axis
  |
  = help: map a variable to `y` where the plot starts, or add the layer that maps it before this one; a line at a place on the other axis is `vline`

== no_axis_for_the_upright_line
error[Z0401]: `vline` draws a line at a place on the `x` axis, but nothing is mapped to `x` yet
 --> scripts/main.zeff:3:19
  |
3 | d.plot(y: change).vline(at: 0)
  |                   ^^^^^ needs an `x` axis
  |
  = help: map a variable to `x` where the plot starts, or add the layer that maps it before this one; a line at a place on the other axis is `hline`

== a_colour_by_a_variable_for_one_line
error[Z0401]: `color:` of `hline` names the variable `arm`, but `at:` is one number: there is one line, and no row to take its colour from
 --> scripts/main.zeff:3:48
  |
3 | d.plot(x: dose, y: change).hline(at: 0, color: arm)
  |                                      - one line
  |                                                ^^^ a colour for each row
  |
  = help: set one colour, as in `color: "firebrick"`, or draw a line for each row of a frame, as in `hline(data: means, at: wage, color: union)`

== another_kind_of_colour
error[Z0401]: the plot shows `arm` as categories for `color`, but `change`, which `vline` maps to `color`, is a Float without value labels, which is shown on a continuous scale
 --> scripts/main.zeff:3:72
  |
3 | d.plot(x: dose, y: change, color: arm).points().vline(at: dose, color: change)
  |                                                                        ^^^^^^ `change` is of another kind
  |
  = help: the layers of a plot share one scale of colour, so the variables mapped to `color` must all be categories (a Category, a Str, a Bool or a variable with value labels) or all be numbers without value labels

== not_a_colour
error[Z0401]: `color:` of `hline` is "redd", which is not the name of a colour
 --> scripts/main.zeff:3:48
  |
3 | d.plot(x: dose, y: change).hline(at: 0, color: "redd")
  |                                                ^^^^^^ not a colour
  |
  = help: did you mean "red"?

== not_a_style
error[Z0402]: `wavy` is not one of the allowed words
 --> scripts/main.zeff:3:48
  |
3 | d.plot(x: dose, y: change).hline(at: 0, style: wavy)
  |                                                ^^^^ expected one of solid, dashed, dotted, dash_dot, long_dash, dash_dot_dot

== a_style_in_quotes
error[Z0403]: expected one of solid, dashed, dotted, dash_dot, long_dash, dash_dot_dot, found text
 --> scripts/main.zeff:3:48
  |
3 | d.plot(x: dose, y: change).hline(at: 0, style: "dashed")
  |                                                ^^^^^^^^ a word, not a string
  |
  = help: write the word without quotes: `dashed`

== no_width
error[Z0401]: `width:` of `vline` is the width of a line in points of 1/72 inch, above 0, but this is 0
 --> scripts/main.zeff:3:48
  |
3 | d.plot(x: dose, y: change).vline(at: 2, width: 0)
  |                                                ^ not a width
  |
  = help: write a width such as 0.25 or 1; without `width:` a reference line is 0.5 wide

== no_linetype_on_a_reference_line
error[Z0404]: `hline` has no argument called `linetype`
 --> scripts/main.zeff:3:41
  |
3 | d.plot(x: dose, y: change).hline(at: 0, linetype: "dashed")
  |                                         ^^^^^^^^ unknown argument
  |
  = help: usage: `p.hline(data: Frame, at: Float | Date | DateTime | Var, color: Var | Str, style: solid | dashed | dotted | dash_dot | long_dash | dash_dot_dot = dashed, width: Float = 0.5)`

